#!/usr/bin/python3
"""kettle-powerd: power, clocks, fan and charging on Kettle Linux's handhelds.

The one writer of CPU/GPU frequency caps, the fan and the battery charge limit. It serves
Steam's power controls through steamos-manager's remote interfaces (remotes.d/kettle-power.toml):

  TdpLimit1             whole-device power budget in watts, held by lowering CPU/GPU caps
  PerformanceProfile1   CPU/GPU caps per profile (device config)
  GpuPerformanceLevel1  auto, or a fixed GPU clock
  BatteryChargeLimit1   charge limit: the charger's end threshold, or held here at the limit,
                        by a charge current of 0 (charge_limit = "current") or the charger's
                        inhibit-charge (charge_limit = "inhibit")
  FanControl1           0: device tree fan curve only, 1: per-game fan settings apply

Steam keeps those per game itself. org.kettlelinux.Power1 adds what Steam has no UI for,
per game (Game Settings' Performance tab): fan curve or fixed speed, per-cluster CPU caps and core
parking; and the charge speed (a preset, or a current of its own) and the fan while charging
asleep (pwm-fan's pwm1_sleep_charging, kernel 40-kettle/1300), for every game. Every cap source is combined here, the lowest wins, so no two writers fight over
scaling_max_freq or devfreq max_freq.

Auto TDP (per game, off by default): the lowest CPU/GPU caps that still hold the game at
Steam's frame rate limit (gamescope's GAMESCOPE_FPS_LIMIT, which Device Settings passes on with
SetFpsLimit), or at the display's refresh rate without one. The frame rate comes from our
mangoapp build's $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kettle-fps (packages/mangohud 0005). It walks the caps down
while the game holds the target, back up as soon as it falls short on a unit at its limit, and keeps off a
step that failed for a while. Steam's TDP limit still applies on top.

  kettle-powerd            run the daemon (system bus, root)
  kettle-powerd --restore  hand the fan back to the kernel and lift every cap, the GPU's to
                           [gpu] auto_max_mhz (ExecStopPost)
"""
import json
import os
import signal
import stat
import sys
import time
import tomllib
import warnings

from gi.repository import Gio, GLib

